text:
Ring out, wild bells, to the wild sky,
The crowds that revel, drink and fight;
The restaurants that run all night;
Ring out, wild bells, and let them die.
Ring out the old, ring in the new;
Ring out the Ducinean jest,
And Vivienne, and all the rest;
Ring out-but let me name few:
Ring out the grief that saps the mind,
For wheezes we have seen before;
The verbal horrors of the war;
The typographs, the cuts unkind.
Ring out the wheezes on the Ford;
And cut the verse of Miss O'Byrne;
Ring in some novel jest, we yearn;
Ring in a tonic for the bored. q



Ring out the pun, the free verse sin,
quote the bard of former times:
"Ring ont, ring out my mournful rhymes,
But ring the fuller minstrel in"


IRWIN.

